      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Emergencies may arise as immediate problems during surgical procedures or they may be delayed sequelae to surgical treatment. The immediate problems include haemorrhage from the operative site; mandibular fracture; tuberosity fracture; fracture of the antral wall; broken instruments; and displaced teeth. The common postoperative complications are swelling due to trauma; infection; and pain. The management of these in the dental office is discussed."},
